THIRD-PARTY RUST NOTICES for librsvg (rsvg-2-2.dll)

Scribobulate's Windows installer redistributes librsvg as bin\rsvg-2-2.dll. That DLL
statically links a graph of Rust crates, which leave no file of their own in the
installed tree -- so shipping librsvg's COPYING.LIB attributes librsvg and nothing it
absorbed. This file is that missing attribution. It does NOT replace COPYING.LIB, which
covers librsvg itself under LGPL-2.1-or-later.

Licences are listed in full below, grouped by licence, naming every crate that uses each.
Note in particular that this graph is not uniformly MIT/Apache: it includes Unicode-3.0
(the icu_* family) and MPL-2.0 (the Servo-lineage CSS crates), each of which carries its
own terms and is listed under its own heading rather than folded into a general
permissive paragraph.

